{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792140725,"nonce":"64nsXXj8qfarBJeoUessUBmCps4=","title":"Apply links: ATS posting behind its own sign-in is treated as a login wall after the walk","message":"From the PR 188 round-4 review (probes in scratchpad/rev188d/probes). 1) Since 9953357 a walk that reaches an ATS posting which 302s to that ATS's own sign-in stores it live, but the sign-in hop stays in the chain, so is_login_link/needs_reresolve are true: the job page shows Open posting, the Apply click goes to the start URL (board copy), it is never re-verified, the nightly reresolve_login_walls re-walks it every night uncounted (about 5 requests per group), and after one bad night it reverts to the board copy and link_rank keeps it there. Fix: when the walk keeps the ATS page, drop or exempt that sign-in hop for is_login_link; same rule in reverify (which now gives blocked where the walk gives live). 2) is_login_wall's path regex matches board slugs like cas, sso, saml, login, so a closed posting redirecting to boards.greenhouse.io/cas?error=true reads live; limit the exemption to each ATS's own sign-in path (Workday /login, Taleo accessmanagement/login.jsf). 3) The on-a-bad-night exemption for named-job hints can store a same-title sibling on the employer site; keep it only for links matched by id number. 0 affected rows today.","files":null}]}